        "content": "In March 2024, development focused almost entirely on MRNIU/opensbi_interface with 18 commits, dominated by feature work and zero pull requests or reviews. The first week accounted for 17 of those commits, introducing C++ macros, cmake install support, QEMU test scaffolding, and function definitions derived from the OpenSBI spec, with subsequent fixes addressing compiler warnings and CMAKE variables. This represents a significant acceleration from the prior period’s 4 commits spread across 4 repos, and a clear shift from the resume-oriented December activity to a concentrated systems‑programming effort. One late‑month commit landed in Simple-XX/SimpleKernel, but the month’s theme remained the structured construction of the OpenSBI interface.",
